<h2>Connect by URL</h2>
<p>In an assistant that supports remote MCP servers, add <strong>{{ serverName }}</strong> with this URL:</p>
<pre><code>{{ endpoint }}</code></pre>
<p>Choose <strong>Streamable HTTP</strong> if asked for a transport, and <strong>No authentication</strong> or <strong>No sign in</strong>. This public connector is read-only.</p>
<h2>Claude</h2>
<p>Open <a href="https://claude.ai/customize/connectors" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Claude connectors</a>, add a custom connector, and enter the name and URL above. Choose no sign in, then enable the connector in your conversation.</p>
<p>Workspace administrators may need to add the connector first. <a href="https://support.claude.com/en/articles/11175166-get-started-with-custom-connectors-using-remote-mcp" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Claude’s setup instructions</a>.</p>
<h2>Other assistants</h2>
<p>Use the same endpoint in ChatGPT or another client that supports custom remote MCP servers. Availability and setup depend on your account and workspace. Your assistant uses its own model to answer, using the records returned by this connector.</p>
<p>Use the public URL above for cloud assistants. They cannot reach a local <code>.wip</code> address on your computer.</p>
